cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A Nominal Formalization of the Confluence of a Calculus with Explicit Substitutions via the Z Property"
abstract: >-
  A formalization in the Rocq Prover (version 9.1.1) of the confluence of the
  lambda-x calculus, an extension of the lambda-calculus with explicit
  substitutions. Terms use a nominal representation, and the proof uses the
  compositional Z property modulo alpha-equivalence. This is the artifact of
  the SBMF 2026 paper with the same title.
authors:
